# fresh_resume_ram_split: A target whose guest RAM differs from the source's. The guest has a root FIFO and task 1, whose pages start at `far`; the image is loaded by guest address, and what the target lacks starts zeroed.   - larger: 128 MiB where there were 64: the resume is the same as     over the same RAM.   - smaller: 512 KiB. The root page, FIFO and task root fit; task 1's     pages (4 MiB in) do not, nor can the guest write there: the     source's own blit, run again, faults the root FIFO in every setup.   - split: the same 64 MiB as two 32 MiB ranges of the memory map     (two host allocations), with task 1's pages straddling the seam.
